🌊 Milestone Update

Today, Project Ocean completed its first end-to-end browser memory cycle.

A memory entered through the browser is now saved to a local vault, retrieved through a Python backend, and rendered back into a searchable timeline.

This may sound simple, but it's an important step toward something much bigger:

Private, continuity-focused AI systems where memory remains owned and controlled by the individual.

One memory at a time.

